<title>USA: Saudi raises Sept crude prices to U.S. by 10 cts.</title>
<headline>Saudi raises Sept crude prices to U.S. by 10 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia has raised September crude export prices to U.S. customers by 10 cents a barrel across the board, trade sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The new formula for Arab Light is West Texas Intermediate/Cushing minus $3.30 a barrel. Arab Medium is WTI minus $4.35, while Arab Heavy is WTI minus $5.20 a barrel.</p>
<p>Berri Extra Light is now $2.60 a barrel under the benchmark.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
